From: Armbian Build Framework <build@armbian.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tools: cgroup: provide a Makefile for the tools clean target

The NVIDIA/Ubuntu 6.8 tree ships tools/cgroup with only Python scripts, but
tools/Makefile's "clean" aggregate descends into tools/cgroup and requires a
"clean" target. Packaging linux-headers therefore fails with:

    make[1]: *** No rule to make target 'clean'.  Stop.
    make: *** [Makefile:173: cgroup_clean] Error 2

Add a minimal Makefile providing the expected clean target.

Signed-off-by: Armbian Build Framework <build@armbian.com>
---
 tools/cgroup/Makefile | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tools/cgroup/Makefile

diff --git a/tools/cgroup/Makefile b/tools/cgroup/Makefile
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..1234567890
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/cgroup/Makefile
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+# tools/cgroup ships only Python scripts; provide the target the top-level
+# tools/Makefile expects when descending into this directory for `clean`.
+clean:
+	@:
-- 
2.43.0
